      "confidence": "needs_confirmation",
      "program_name": "Affordable Housing Impact Fee and Inclusionary Requirements (County Code Chapter 18.107)",
      "administering_agency": "Napa County Housing and Community Services; Planning, Building and Environmental Services",
      "funding_type": "regulatory requirement",
      "typical_award_size": "Not a subsidy; it capitalizes the Affordable Housing Fund. Fees adopted Oct 21, 2025 (3-2 vote), effective Jan 16, 2026, phased 50% in 2026, 75% in 2027, 100% in 2028: residential per sq ft $0 up to 2,500 sq ft, $43 for 2,501-3,500 sq ft (was $10.75), $86 above 3,500 sq ft (was $12.25); ADUs under 751 sq ft exempt. Nonresidential per sq ft: hotel $100 (was $9), retail and restaurant $58.40 (was $7.50), office $14.68 (was $5.25), industrial $7.70 (was $4.50), warehouse $7.50 (was $3.60).",
      "per_unit_cap": null,
      "affordability_requirement": "Ownership projects: 20% of single-family detached units or 17% of attached units for moderate income (120% AMI) households, 40-year restrictions. Rental projects pay housing fees or elect the alternative of 12% of units at low income rents under a rent regulatory agreement. Exempt: farmworker units of 1,200 sq ft or less, 100% affordable projects, certain multifamily and SRO projects, projects of four or fewer units may pay a per-unit fee. Equivalency proposals (off-site units, land dedication) allowed with Planning Commission approval.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "Fees apply to applications filed after Jan 15, 2026 at 50% of the new schedule; 75% in 2027; full schedule in 2028. The Board also directed staff to create a fee deferral program for owners who rent units as affordable housing; terms not yet published.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "unclear",
      "layering_notes": "Relevant to developers two ways: 100% affordable multifamily is exempt from the fee, and the fee stream funds the County Affordable Housing Fund. A fee exemption or waiver can count as public funds under Labor Code 1720(b)(4), so confirm prevailing wage exposure with counsel. Applies only in unincorporated Napa County; each city has its own inclusionary and linkage rules (Pass 3). Code text was read from the Zoneomics mirror (Ordinances 1334 of 2010, 1386 of 2013, 1491 of June 4, 2024 and 1495 of Sept 24, 2024); fee amounts come from Sonoma Index-Tribune and CBS Bay Area coverage of the Oct 21, 2025 vote. napacounty.gov pages and DocumentCenter PDFs sit behind Cloudflare and refused automated access on 2026-11-06, so the county's own page could not be opened; the official FAQ is https://www.napacounty.gov/3951/Affordable-Housing-Impact-Fee-Housing-Co.",
      "source_url": "https://www.zoneomics.com/code/napa-county-unincorporated-CA/chapter_36",
      "record_id": "a222ce7fbf",
      "cycle_notes": "",
      "eligible_project_detail": [
        "new construction"
      ],
      "next_deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_check": "no_date",
      "link_status": "ok",
      "audit_note": "Official Legistar record (matter 25-1814, Resolution R-2025-114) confirms the Oct 21, 2025 hearing, 3-2 vote (Ramos, Manfree, Gallagher yes; Alessio, Cottrell no) and Jan 16, 2026 effective date, but the motion was approved as amended and the amended fee table is not posted. The pre-hearing draft resolution set residential ownership fees at $0/sq ft for 0-2,000 sq ft, $43 for 2,001-3,000 and $86 above 3,000; residential rental $0/sq ft; office $14.50, hotel $100, retail/restaurant $58.40, industrial and warehouse $7.75, with annual CCI indexing. The record's tiers (2,500/3,500 sq ft), phase-in and office/industrial/warehouse rates come from news coverage and could not be matched to an official document. napacounty.gov and municode are Cloudflare-blocked and the code text is only on the Zoneomics mirror. The draft rental fee of $0/sq ft conflicts with the record's statement that rental projects pay housing fees.",
      "last_audited": "2026-11-08"
    }
  },
