      "program_name": "HOME and CDBG, Napa County (state non-entitlement status)",
      "administering_agency": "California HCD state HOME and CDBG programs; Napa County Housing and Community Services as applicant",
      "funding_type": "grant",
      "typical_award_size": "None directly. Napa County is not a HUD CDBG entitlement urban county or a HOME participating jurisdiction. The City of Napa is the only CDBG entitlement in the county (FY 2024-25 entitlement $583,519) and draws HOME and ESG through State HCD grants. No County of Napa state HOME or CDBG award for 2024 or 2025 surfaced in HCD award lists.",
      "per_unit_cap": "HOME per-unit subsidy limits (24 CFR 92.250) apply to any state HOME award.",
      "affordability_requirement": "State HOME: 20% of HOME units at 50% AMI, rest at 60% AMI, 55-year HCD covenant. State CDBG: 51% of units for households at or below 80% AMI.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "acquisition-rehab",
        "preservation"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "annual NOFA",
      "next_deadline": "Follow HCD state HOME and CDBG NOFAs (state records). A developer in unincorporated Napa or the four small cities needs the County or city to apply as the state HOME or CDBG grantee.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "There is no county-level HOME or CDBG pipeline to layer in Napa; this is a negative finding. The City of Napa CDBG and HOME programs are Pass 3. Napa County received $207,965 of State ESG for CA-517 in the 2024 NOFA, usable for shelter and rapid rehousing, not capital. HOME and CDBG carry federal Davis-Bacon (CDBG at 8+ units, HOME at 12+ units) and state prevailing wage. Status inferred from the City of Napa 2025-2030 Consolidated Plan, the City FY 2024-25 CAPER and HCD award lists; confirm with the County.",
      "source_url": "https://www.cityofnapa.org/DocumentCenter/View/14570/DRAFT-City-of-Napa-2025-2030-Consolidated-Plan",
      "record_id": "88123f77f8",
      "cycle_notes": "",
      "eligible_project_detail": [
        "new construction",
        "acquisition-rehab",
        "preservation"
      ],
      "next_deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_check": "no_date",
      "link_status": "ok",
      "audit_note": "The City of Napa 2025-2030 Consolidated Plan confirms the City is the CDBG entitlement (about $591,000 a year average over FY 2025-29) and receives no direct HOME, ESG or HOPWA, but it says nothing about County entitlement status and lists HOME as administered in partnership with Napa County, which cuts against the record's statement that no county-level HOME pipeline exists. The $583,519 FY 2024-25 figure and the absence of County state HOME/CDBG awards were not found in the documents opened; confirm with HUD CPD allocation tables and HCD award lists.",
      "last_audited": "2026-11-08"
