      "program_name": "Napa fee deferral and reduced building permit fees for affordable and workforce housing (Housing Element Programs H2-2.8 and H2-1.1)",
      "administering_agency": "City of Napa Community Development Department (Building Division) and Housing Division",
      "funding_type": "fee waiver",
      "typical_award_size": "Resolution R2021-119 (adopted Dec 7, 2021) sets building permit fees (plan review and inspection) at 50% of the R2021-105 schedule for each Affordable and Workforce Housing Unit: units sold or rented at affordable cost to households at or below 120% AMI under an NMC 15.94.080 affordable housing agreement, and ADUs of 500 sq ft or less (fee numbers 2.1.6-2.1.10 multifamily, 2.1.26-2.1.30 single family, 2.1.36 ADU). Separately, the City has a documented practice of deferring impact fees to occupancy for qualifying affordable projects (Prohousing matrix item 3C). Housing Element Program H2-2.8 (fees deferred, reduced or waived plus fast tracking for 100% affordable projects) was reported as not initiated in the 2023 APR.",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not applicable; percentage reduction of permit fees, no dollar cap published.",
      "affordability_requirement": "Affordable and workforce housing at or below 120% AMI per the reported 2021 action; impact fee deferral applies to affordable units as defined in NMC 15.94 (80% AMI or below).",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "mixed-income",
        "adu"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "Applied at permit issuance on request. Confirm the current master fee schedule discount and the status of the H2-2.8 fast track program with the Building Division (NapaON permit portal) before underwriting; Housing Element fee realignment is due by 2028.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "unclear",
      "layering_notes": "Fee relief is modest relative to the impact fee and TOT loans but is routinely combined with them. Napa Valley Unified School District and Napa Sanitation District fees are outside the City's control. Waived or reduced fees can count as public funds under Labor Code 1720(b)(4), so confirm with counsel. The Prohousing matrix (source_url) and the Housing Element were opened; the 50% figure comes from news coverage and is marked needs_confirmation.",
      "source_url": "https://www.cityofnapa.org/DocumentCenter/View/12551/Final-Prohousing-Designation-Matrix-PDF",
      "record_id": "3ae88136e6",
      "cycle_notes": "",
      "eligible_project_detail": [
        "new construction",
        "100% affordable projects",
        "adu",
        "mixed-income projects"
      ],
      "next_deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_check": "no_date",
      "link_status": "ok",
      "audit_note": "The 50% permit fee reduction is now confirmed from the City's own Resolution R2021-119 on Legistar (matter 400-2021, adopted Dec 7, 2021); whether the current master fee schedule carries it forward past the R2021-105 schedule years (2022-2024) was not confirmed. Prevailing wage left unclear: no City rule addresses it, and Labor Code 1720(b)(4) fee reductions are subject to 1720(c) exemptions and de minimis limits that no source applies here.",
